  <content_rating type="oars-1.1" />
  <releases>
    <release version="0.8.0" date="2026-11-07" type="stable">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.8.0</url>
      <description>
        <p>You can now look things up on the web and check calculations without leaving your chat. With a compatible Ollama or Ollama Cloud model, turn on Web or Calculator in Chat Settings, or type /web or /calculator. Web uses DuckDuckGo by default, without a search account, and you can choose another search service in Preferences. It asks for permission first and stays off in Local Only mode. Sources and tool results stay with your chats when you return to them, export them or continue in a new chat.</p>
        <p>The redesigned Models view helps you find a model for everyday questions, coding, pictures or documents. Filters let you narrow the choices, and model details show download size and estimated memory and storage needs. If Moose manages Ollama, suggestions also consider the memory available on your computer. You can start a chat with an installed model right away, and progress messages make downloads and removals easier to follow.</p>
        <p>OpenRouter is now available as another way to chat. Add your key and choose a model, with pictures and reasoning options where supported. We've also made it easier to switch between services and find your chat settings. Chat titles now better reflect your topic and language.</p>
        <p>Longer chats with Ollama now leave more room for an answer. If an answer stops because it reaches its length limit, the text stays saved and you can choose Continue to pick up where it stopped. Moose remembers your reasoning preference, with reasoning off by default where supported. We've also improved message spacing to make conversations easier to read.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.7.5" date="2026-10-29" type="stable">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.7.5</url>
      <description>
        <p>Download compatible GGUF models from Hugging Face through your Ollama connection. Paste a model link, an Ollama model name or an ollama run or ollama pull command, and optionally choose a quantization or GGUF filename.</p>
        <p>Start a new chat from a completed download or use an already installed model from the download dialog. Failed downloads offer an Edit and Retry action with clearer guidance, and download progress now clears when a transfer finishes, fails or is cancelled.</p>
        <p>The initial setup now opens the provider chooser so you can select a local or cloud connection. Chat bubble backgrounds display correctly with custom GTK themes, and model search fits better in narrow windows.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.7.0" date="2026-10-22" type="stable">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.7.0</url>
      <description>
        <p>You can now check for updates, update or repair the Ollama installation managed by Moose right from Preferences. Your models and chats stay put. This release comes with Ollama 0.40.6, lets you pick up interrupted engine downloads and brings back the previous installation if an update fails.</p>
        <p>We've tidied up the setup screens for local and cloud providers. If something goes wrong, you can view and copy Moose and Ollama logs from Diagnostics, or copy the details of a model download or deletion. If a model needs a newer Ollama version, Moose offers to update its managed installation and try the download again.</p>
        <p>Tables now fit better in chats and have a button to copy them as Markdown. We also fixed chat bubble sizing. When selecting a long passage, you can drag toward the edge of the chat to scroll and keep selecting.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.6.5" date="2026-10-20" type="stable">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.6.5</url>
      <description>
        <p>Connect to NVIDIA NIM and Cloudflare Workers AI, with model discovery, streamed responses, reasoning and image support on compatible models. Model IDs containing spaces now work with compatible cloud providers and custom connections.</p>
        <p>Select text more reliably and read Markdown, code and formulas as answers arrive, with scrolling that lets you review earlier content. Chat messages now size correctly, and completed responses remain visible if saving fails.</p>
        <p>Managed Ollama now stops when Moose closes and prevents conflicting instances from using the same installation. Model downloads report provider errors and incomplete transfers instead of appearing to finish successfully.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.6.1" date="2026-10-16" type="stable">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.6.1</url>
      <description>
        <p>Connect to Mistral AI and DeepSeek, or add a custom cloud provider with your own server address and authentication settings.</p>
        <p>Discover models automatically or add them manually, with image support configurable for each saved model.</p>
        <p>This update also adds reasoning controls for supported Mistral and DeepSeek models and fixes managed Ollama installation in folders accessed through symbolic links.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.6.0" date="2026-10-06" type="stable">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.6.0</url>
      <description>
        <p>Connect securely to cloud providers using your own API key and control what you share.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Enable Local Only mode to restrict inference to Ollama managed by Moose.</li>
          <li>Allow messages in all chats with a provider or ask in each chat. File sharing requires separate permission. Review context before sending and reset permissions in Privacy settings.</li>
          <li>Open Files from the sidebar to browse, search and filter attachments and library documents. Preview files, find their original folder, reopen related chats or attach them to the current chat.</li>
          <li>Browse more local models for chat, vision, reasoning and coding.</li>
          <li>See clearer waiting and reasoning indicators that disappear when the answer starts arriving.</li>
          <li>External Ollama connections now require HTTPS, with HTTP available only for connections on this device.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.5.0" date="2026-09-26" type="stable">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.5.0</url>
      <description>
        <p>Bring images and documents into your conversations. Attach photos, PDFs, text and code, or search your local document library with source excerpts and page references.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Edit messages in place, regenerate answers and switch between saved versions or continue in a separate chat.</li>
          <li>View model reasoning separately and choose the reasoning options supported by your model.</li>
          <li>Keep drafts and attachments between sessions, move between chats during a response and receive a completion notification.</li>
          <li>Review model download history, retry interrupted downloads and keep chatting while a model downloads.</li>
          <li>Read mathematical formulas with local rendering, scrolling for long expressions and access to the original LaTeX.</li>
          <li>Use a wider, aligned chat and composer, compact model controls, clearer attachment previews and helpful starting suggestions.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.4.3" date="2026-06-17">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.4.3</url>
      <description>
        <p>Adds GPU acceleration support for managed Ollama through Vulkan when available.</p>
        <p>Adds a managed hardware preference so GPU acceleration can be enabled or disabled.</p>
        <p>Shows the active managed Ollama acceleration backend in the provider status.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.4.2" date="2026-06-16">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.4.2</url>
      <description>
        <p>Adds configurable keyboard shortcuts for common chat, model and navigation actions.</p>
        <p>Adds a shortcuts page to preferences so shortcuts can be changed, cleared or reset.</p>
        <p>Shows when the active conversation is generating a response in the conversation list.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.4.1" date="2026-06-15">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.4.1</url>
      <description>
        <p>Adds tools to organize conversation history so older chats are easier to review and manage.</p>
        <p>Adds conversation export support for saving chats outside Moose.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.4.0" date="2026-06-15">
      <description>
        <p>Conversations now include recent message history so models can follow the thread.</p>
        <p>Adds per-chat settings for system prompts, preferred models, context limits and Ollama generation options.</p>
        <p>Introduces built-in chat profiles and reusable custom profiles that stay on your device.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.3.1" date="2026-05-29">
      <description>
        <p>Improves the sidebar and provider switcher with a cleaner layout.</p>
        <p>Fixes visual bugs that appeared when using light mode.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.3.0" date="2026-05-28">
      <url type="details">https://github.com/moooossee/moose/releases/tag/v0.3.0</url>
      <description>
        <p>Moose now renders chat messages with Markdown formatting for clearer model responses.</p>
        <p>Code blocks include syntax highlighting, line numbers and a copy action so generated code is easier to read and reuse.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.2.1" date="2026-05-27">
      <description>
        <p>Moose now opens just once when launched from Flathub.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.2.0" date="2026-05-22">
      <description>
        <p>Adds Moose-managed Ollama so the Flatpak works without a host Ollama installation.</p>
        <p>Fresh installs can create an instance, download a model and chat. Nice.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.0" date="2026-05-17">
      <description>
        <p>First version of Moose, with local Ollama chat, saved conversations, provider settings and basic model management.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
  <supports>
    <control>keyboard</control>
    <control>pointing</control>
  </supports>
  <requires>
    <display_length compare="ge">768</display_length>
  </requires>
</component>
